<title>USA: U.S. 5-year note auction high yield 6.024 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. 5-year note auction high yield 6.024 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Treasury said its Dutch bidding auction of 5-year notes produced these results:</p>
<p>			 5-YEAR NOTES DUE JULY 31, 2002</p>
<p>			     $11.501 BILLION AUCTION</p>
<p>	     YIELD			  PRICE	COUPON</p>
<p> HIGH	6.024    Awarded At	99.898	6.000</p>
<p> MEDIAN    6.017    High Yield	NOT GIVEN  Percent</p>
<p> LOW	 5.950    87 Percent	NOT GIVEN</p>
<p>	   Cover - (Bids Over Amount Sold)    =  2.88 Times</p>
<p> U.S. TREASURY (GOVERNMENT DEBT)		 MATURITY 31.JUL.02</p>
<p> MATURITY/TYPE    5-YEAR NOTES		   PAY DATE 31.Jul.97</p>
<p> TYPE OF DEBT     STRAIGHT			 LAUNCHED 23.Jun.97</p>
<p> ISSUED/ACCEPTED  11.501 BLN USD		 CUSIP    9128273C4</p>
<p> BIDS SUBMITTED   33.115			   COUNTRY	  USA</p>
<p> NONCOMPETITIVE   473.84 MLN			  DUTCH AUCTION</p>
<p> NY FED DISTRICT    N.A.			   COUPON	 6.000</p>
<p> FOREIGN INSTITN  410.00 MLN		     PRICE	 99.898</p>
<p> BIDDING RANGE    5.950-6.024 PCT		YIELD-HIGH   6.024</p>
<p>KEY (HIGH) YIELD DOWN FROM 6.298 PCT AT AUCTION ON 25.JUN.97 KEY (HIGH) YIELD LOWEST SINCE 5.950 PCT AT AUCTION 20.NOV.96</p>
